<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Green Vault</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Grünes Gewölbe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Green Vault (Grünes Gewölbe) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a> is the treasury museum of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a>, created by Augustus the Strong between 1723 and 1730 in rooms of Dresden Castle. It displays one of the largest collections of precious objects in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, including works by the court jeweller Johann Melchior Dinglinger. A theft of eighteenth-century jewellery from it in 2019 drew worldwide attention.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/green-vault.jpg" alt="Green Vault" width="320" height="476" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Slick · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dresden_2012-05-22-6590.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
